      <div type="clause" n="El. 25">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 25</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 25" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="34" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif ðeof brece mannes hús nihtes ⁊ he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.30"/> weorðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.31"/> þær ofslegen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.32"/>, ne sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.1"/> he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.33"/> na mansleges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.34"/> scyldig.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="††" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.dagger2"/> Gif he siððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.1"/> æfter sunnan upgonge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.2"/> þis deð, he bið mansleges scyldig ⁊ he ðonne self<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.3"/> swelte, buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.4"/> he nieddæda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.5"/> wære.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.6"/> Gif mid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.7"/> him cwicum sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.8"/> funden þæt he ǽr stæl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.9"/>, be twyfealdum forgielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.10"/> hit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 25" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="34" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif ðeof brece mannes hus nihtes ⁊ he weorðe ðær ofslagen, ne sy he mansleges scyldig. Gif he siðða<hi rend="italic">n<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.1-4"/></hi> æfter sunnan úpgange þis deð, he bið mansleges scyldig ⁊ he ðonne sylf swelte, butan he nieddæda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.2-2"/> wære. Gyf mid him cwicu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> sie funden þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ær stæl, be twyfealdum forgylde he hit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 25" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="35" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif þeof brece mannes hus nihtes ⁊ he wurðe ðær ofslegen, ne sy he na<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.1-2"/> mansleges scyldig. Gif he syððan æfter sunnan uppgange ðis deð, he biþ mansleges scyldig ⁊ he þonne swylte, butan he nyddæde wære. Gif mid him cwycu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> sy funden þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ær stæl, be twyfealdu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> forgylde hit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 25" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="35" ed="#liebermann"/>Si effringens fur domum uel effodiens fuerit inuentus et accepto uulnere mortuus fuerit, percussor non erit reus sanguinis. Quodsi orto sole hoc fecerit et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.1-3"/> homicidium perpetrauerit, et ipse morietur. Si non habuerit quod pro furto reddat, uenundabitur. Si inuentum fuerit apud eum quod furatus est uiuens, siue bos siue asinus siue ouis, duplum restituet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 25" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="248" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif ðeof brece mannes hús nihtes ⁊ he weorðe þær ofslegen, ne sie he na mansleges scyldig. Gif he siððan æfter sunnan upgonge þis deð, he bið mansleges scyldig ⁊ he ðonne self swelte, buton he nieddæda wære. Gif mid him cwicum sie funden þæt he ær stæl, be twyfealdum forgielde hit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="35" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein Dieb jemandes Haus nachts<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.1"/> erbricht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.2"/> und dort erschlagen wird, so sei er [der<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.3"/> ihn tödtete] nicht Todtschlages schuldig. Wenn dieser später nach Sonnenaufgang das thut, ist er Todtschlages schuldig und er sterbe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.4"/> dann selbst, ausser<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.5"/> wenn er in Nothwehr handelte. Wenn bei ihm, dem lebenden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.6"/> [Diebe], was er früher gestohlen hatte, gefunden wird, vergelte er dies zwiefach.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a thief breaks into someone’s house at night and is slain there, then let him [who killed him] not be guilty of manslaughter. If the latter does this later, after sunrise, he is guilty of manslaughter and let him then die himself, unless he acted in self-defence. If what he had stolen earlier is found with him, the living [thief], let him repay it twofold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="249" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a thief should break into a man’s house at night and be slain there, let him [the slayer] not [be deemed] culpable for the homicide. If he does this after sunrise, he will be culpable for the homicide; and let him suffer death himself, unless he were constrained by necessity [in killing the thief]. If, while he [the thief] lives, that which he has stolen is found, let him pay twice its value.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 22,2–4</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="35, 37">Exodus 22.2; Exodus 22.3; Exodus 22.4</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[22, 2] | [22, 3] | [22, 4]</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><ref target="clause:Ine_16">Ine 16</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">weorð <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> wyrþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">weorð So; wyrþe Ld</seg></note>
