        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">36</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">siððā</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">siððā</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">36</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">alt?</hi>) <hi rend="italic">geänd. aus</hi> -de</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(old?) altered from -de</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nächtlichkeit als Qualifikation der Missetat entnahm Af wohl dem folgenden Exodus-Verse. Sie fehlt Agsä. Rechte. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> über Af’s Angleichung der Bibel an dieses <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Diebstahl 22a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af probably took night-time as an aggravating qualification of the misdeed from the following verse of Exodus. It is lacking in A.-S. law. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> on Af’s assimilation of the Bible to this law <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Diebstahl 22a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Einbruch 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Einbruch 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ld aus Vulgata; ‘niemand des Totschlags an ihm’ So</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ld from the Vulgate; ‘no one of homicide on him’ So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gegen Agsä. Recht, daher durch Af in folgender Zeile aufgehoben</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Contrary to Anglo-Saxon law, hence cancelled by Af in the following line</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bessere Übs.: ‘unter Zwang’ laut <hi rend="italic">Wb: nieddæda; vgl. Gl</hi> Notwehr 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Better transl.: ‘under compulsion’, according to <hi rend="italic">Wb: nieddæda; cf. Gl</hi> Notwehr 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Af missversteht <hi rend="italic">uiuens</hi> der Vulg., das Adjektiv zum Gestohlenen, vom Diebe und sieht darin den Ggs. zur Erschlagung des handhaft Ertappten (nicht etwa zur Bussschuld auch seiner Erben)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af misunderstands the <hi rend="italic">uiuens</hi> of the Vulg., the adjective qualifying the stolen thing, as referring to the thief, and sees in it the contrast to the slaying of a thief caught in the act (not, say, to the liability of his heirs too to pay compensation)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-25.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> El 24¹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> El 24¹</seg></note>
      </div>
